From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:59:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wintypes: add DataReader, and the rest of DataWriter.

DataWriter wrote bytes and nothing else.  It now writes every type, in the
byte order it is given (big-endian until told otherwise), strings as UTF-8
or UTF-16 of either order, measures them, flushes and closes its stream,
and says what it is.  A GUID is written the way Windows writes it: its
three leading fields in the byte order, the last eight bytes as one 64-bit
integer.

DataReader is new: from a buffer (read in place, and handed back compacted
by DetachBuffer) or from a stream it loads from.  A read past what is
loaded fails with E_BOUNDS and consumes nothing, bytes that are not UTF-8
fail with ERROR_NO_UNICODE_TRANSLATION, and a closed reader answers
RO_E_CLOSED, as they do on Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0e31b1a8c6d3bcb968f3aa1da56f366bacdede58)

